        "entry_bhNUAF": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do babies really start life without bacteria?",
            "caption": "<p>Yes, newborns enter the world with a nearly sterile gut. Their microbiome starts developing through birth, breastfeeding and close contact. Probiotics help support that process from day one.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_XTmgVR": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do these probiotics help with colic, gas, or digestive discomfort?",
            "caption": "<p>By introducing beneficial bacteria, Lovebug helps gently rebalance your baby's gut—reducing gas, easing colic, and supporting smoother digestion for a calmer, more comfortable baby.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_A4ptwU": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why are probiotics especially important in the first year?",
            "caption": "<p>The first 1,000 days are when your baby's gut and immune system is growing the fastest. Daily probiotics help guide that development, supporting smoother digestion and stronger immune balance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_LUmytY": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it safe to give every day?",
            "caption": "<p>Yes, probiotic drops are safe for full-term babies from day one. Lovebug baby probiotic drops are gentle enough for newborns and made with organic ingredients.</p><p>They're designed for daily use to keep good bacteria steady as your baby grows. Probiotics are not recommended for pre-term infants who have special health needs and should be cared for under medical supervision.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_LUyb3e": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "When is the best time of day to give them?",
            "caption": "<p>Any time works—just stay consistent. Many parents prefer giving drops during or after a feeding for ease and routine.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_Tk7kc7": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How long does it take for probiotic drops to start working?",
            "caption": "<p>Many parents notice subtle improvements in just a few days, with more consistent digestive support developing over 1–2 weeks of daily use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_iF7D7i": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What are the signs that they're working?",
            "caption": "<p>Look for small but meaningful changes: less gas and fussiness, more regularity, greater comfort after feeding and improved overall calmness.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_yALnDh": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What makes Lovebug Baby Probiotic Drops different from other baby probiotics?",
            "caption": "<p>Lovebug is designed with intention. We have targeted, baby specific strains, an exceptionally clean formulation that is certified organic which provides gentle, effective support for your baby.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_D39bNC": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if my baby was born by C-section or needed antibiotics?",
            "caption": "<p>Those early experiences can sometimes reduce the amount of beneficial bacteria baby receives, adding probiotics can help restore balance and support a healthier gut environment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_KtrrDa": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why do practitioners recommend Lovebug Baby Probiotic drops?",
            "caption": "<p>Practitioners trust Lovebug for its science-backed strains, purity standards, and gentle effectiveness—making it a reliable choice for supporting infant gut health from the very beginning.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_MzM3b9": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do they need to be kept in the fridge?",
            "caption": "<p>Only if you like them cold! They should be stored in a cool, dry place. All of our probiotics have a 2 year shelf life from time of manufacture.</p>"
          }
        },
        "entry_dgbmCy": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What if it doesn't work?",
            "caption": "<p>You're covered by our 30-day money back guarantee. Try it risk free!</p>"
          }
        }
      },
